# Default extraction output when following this README's example commands.
# bin/ and obj/ are already covered by the repo root .gitignore.
#
# out/conformance/claims/ is the one exception: it is hand-maintained migration work
# product (conformance-schema.md: "Claims are human work product accumulated across a
# migration -- which decisions were made, by whom, and why"), never regenerated by
# ssisx, and worthless if it isn't committed. A blanket "out/" would silently discard it
# on a fresh clone or a regenerated --out dir. Git can't negate a path whose parent
# directory is itself excluded, hence the explicit re-inclusion of each ancestor below.
out/*
!out/conformance/
out/conformance/*
!out/conformance/claims/
out-*/

# scripts/ ships Run-Survey.ps1 + Run-Survey.bat to a client machine alongside a
# self-contained ssisx.exe -- Publish-Survey.ps1 builds that exe (and its ~200 runtime
# DLLs) directly into this folder, and a survey run writes its own output (ssis-survey/,
# ssis-survey-EXPORT/, ssis-survey-EXPORT.zip) there too. The two wrapper scripts are
# source and belong in git; everything else in this folder is build/run output
# (rebuildable on demand, and in the survey output's case, someone's real portfolio
# data) and none of it does.
scripts/*
!scripts/*.ps1
!scripts/*.bat
